def two_sum(nums: list[int], target: int) -> list[int]:
    seen = {}
    for i, num in enumerate(nums):
        complement = target - num
        if complement in seen:
            return [seen[complement], i]
        seen[num] = i
```

This runs in O(n) time and O(n) space by storing each number's index as you scan. When you encounter a number whose complement is already stored, you've found the pair. Since the input is guaranteed to have exactly one solution, the first match returned is the answer.
